{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-71811-r4523318","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Atomic Fudge Cake","sourcePageId":71811,"sourceRevision":"4523318","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-07-13T17:35:36Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Atomic%20Fudge%20Cake&oldid=4523318","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:22:55.272Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baking recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for cake","Category:Recipes for dessert","Category:Recipes using baking powder","Category:Recipes using baking soda","Category:Recipes using cocoa powder","Category:Recipes using cow milk","Category:Recipes using dark chocolate","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using powdered sugar","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Recipes using whipping cream","Category:Recipes using white sugar","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"b58dee78b3ab11c52b6decfe232f96fbfe86e0c8cb059facfc0a80afc62d3bb2","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Cake recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n| Image = [[File:Atomicfudge1.JPG|300px]]\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Desserts|Desserts]]\n\nA rich chocolate [[Cookbook:Cake|cake]] recipe.\n\n==Ingredients==\n=== Cake ===\n*2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] (470 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]]) white [[cookbook:sugar|sugar]]\n*1 ¾ cup (415 ml) [[cookbook:flour|flour]]\n*1 ¾ cups (415 ml) baking [[cookbook:cocoa|cocoa]] powder\n*1 ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] (7 ml) [[cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n*1 ½ teaspoon (7 ml) [[cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n*1 teaspoon [[cookbook:salt|salt]] (5ml)\n*2 [[cookbook:egg|eggs]]\n*1 cup (235 ml) [[cookbook:milk|milk]]\n*½ cup (120 ml) [[cookbook:Vegetable Oil|vegetable oil]]\n*2 teaspoons (10 ml) [[cookbook:Vanilla Extract|vanilla extract]]\n*1 cup (235 ml) boiling [[cookbook:water|water]]\n\n=== Frosting ===\n*⅛ cup (30 ml) [[cookbook:cocoa|cocoa]]\n*7 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]] (200 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) [[cookbook:Dark chocolate|dark chocolate]]\n*⅛ cup (30 ml) boiling [[cookbook:water|water]]\n*1/16 cup (15 ml) [[cookbook:Powdered Sugar|powdered sugar]]\n*⅔ cup (156 ml) [[cookbook:Cream|whipping cream]]\n== Procedure ==\n\n=== Cake ===\n#Mix the dry ingredients well in a large bowl. For better texture, sift the dry ingredients together with a sieve or sifter.\n#Add the eggs, milk, vanilla, and vegetable oil, and mix well. Add the water, and mix it until it has a lot of little bubbles. This batter will be very thin.\n#Pour into two greased 9-inch round [[Cookbook:Cake Pan|baking pans]].\n#[[cookbook:Bake|Bake]] in a preheated [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] at 180°C for 30 minutes (about 20 minutes for a convection oven), or until a cake tester comes out clean. Remember not to over-bake the cake, as it may become really dry and lose all its moisture.\n#Cool the cakes completely, then unmold them.\n=== Frosting ===\n#Melt the chocolate by placing it in a [[Cookbook:Double Boiler|double boiler]].\n#Mix the sugar and cocoa together in a small bowl, then mix in the water.\n#Stir the sugar/cocoa/water mix into the melted chocolate.\n#Quickly stir in the cream and mix until it has a smooth consistency.\n#Immediately 'frost' the cake with this, making sure that there is quite a bit between the two layers of cake. The cake will need to be refrigerated to harden the fudge, so don't worry about its relatively liquid nature.\n#Refrigerate cake.\n#Serve warm after refrigeration. To serve, slice a piece and microwave it for about 20 seconds. The fudge will melt and soak into the cake. Serve with ice cream if you so desire.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* Higher quality chocolate and baking cocoa will make a noticeable difference in the cake's overall quality.\n* A hot fudge sauce to go over top of the cake can be a nice extra touch.\n* Don't try and substitute unsweetened chocolate for the dark chocolate.\n* Spices such as [[cookbook:cinnamon|cinnamon]] can be added to the frosting if desired.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for cake|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dark chocolate]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes with images]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using white sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using powdered sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cocoa powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using whipping cream]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cow milk]]","isRecipe":false,"recipe":{"name":"Atomic Fudge Cake","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[],"steps":[],"nutrition":null,"gaps":["Research extraction only; no culinary/editorial review.","Ingredient quantities, units, alternatives, food identities, aggregate duration, and nutrition remain unknown until individually parsed/reviewed.","Source-level CC BY-SA policy applies generally; page-specific exceptions have not been checked."]}},"parsedRecipe":{"s